# which slice of time the browsed set is cut to: "today", "week", "month" or
# "all". A preference and not a position, so it is user-scoped and follows the
# person to their other devices — unlike /browse's `view` and `open`, which are
# where-you-are and stay on the device that chose them.
#
# The default is "all", so a newcomer on a quiet day does not open the app to
# an empty map. That is a call and not a reading of the ask; it is this line.
period: String = "all".to_string() (user, last-write, own)
# the three local midnights, "<today>,<week>,<month>" in epoch milliseconds,
# computed by the page half and sent in as a SinceMarks event. A day start is a
# fact about THIS phone's clock and zone and belongs to nobody else, so it is
# device-scoped; empty means "not told yet", and the filter keeps everything
# until it is.
day_starts: String = String::new() (device, last-write, own)
